In article <8447@star.cs.vu.nl> lbkruij@cs.vu.nl (Kruijswijk Lucas B) writes:

>A wizard monster can cast a curse spell (like punishment). However if you

Take care thing of such a thing... Tim Brown, who earlier advocated the iron
ball as a blessing in disguise is not prepared to go as far as to suggest that
monsters should hand them out willy-nilly!  With one iron ball you have a
powerful tool, sacrificing the ability to carry the billions of black knives
one finds lying around and maybe a 1st level Knight's armour, but when a monster
can make the thing twice as heavy (as per second scroll of punishment) then
you're sunk.  To be able to move with a heavy(*2) iron ball, you are sure to
need experience.  To gain experience you have to run around the dungeon killing
monsters.  As you see, this put one in the same impossible situation as a
cursed ring of levitation (I put one of these on at level 20 and almost cried!)

Anyhow, if a monster is capable of causing punishment more than once, it may as
well have the cockatrice's touch!  Given the limited number of curses that could
exist and the current rules concerning scrolls of punishment, one would be bound
to be cursed with punishment twice before finding a scroll of remove curse.

OK, to me this is when the thing becomes a real cuse instead of a blessing, but
it also makes the game impossible for lower level characters (there again, when
was it ever easy?).

